{red|**Identify your main co-parenting challenges.**

What makes co-parenting difficult for you?}{red| Where does conflict with your ex most affect your children?}{red| What do your children need that is hard to provide given your co-parenting situation?}{red| What would improve if you could change one thing about your co-parenting?}

Write about your co-parenting challenges:

{red|**Honestly assess how well you are shielding your children from conflict.**

Are there ways you have exposed them to adult conflict?}{red| Have you used them as messengers, confidants, or in other inappropriate roles?}{red| What do your children see and hear about your conflict with your ex?}{red| Where do you need to improve in protecting them?}

Write your shielding assessment:

{red|**Assess your current communication with your co-parent.**

What methods do you currently use to communicate?}{red| What works well?}{red| What leads to conflict?}{red| How often does communication stay focused on children versus drift to other issues?}{red| What would improve your co-parent communication?}

Write your communication assessment:

{red|**Assess the consistency between your two homes.**

What is consistent across both homes?}{red| What is significantly different?}{red| What differences seem to be hardest on your children?}{red| What areas would benefit most from more consistency?}{red| What is realistic to align given your co-parenting relationship?}

Write your consistency assessment:

{red|**Reflect on how your children are adjusting to the divorce.**

What signs of grief or struggle have you noticed in each child?}{red| How is each child responding differently?}{red| What have you done to support their adjustment?}{red| What do you think they need that you have not been providing?}

Write about your children's adjustment:

{red|**Assess the level of conflict in your co-parenting relationship.**

Is your co-parenting relationship genuinely high-conflict or difficult but manageable?}{red| What specific behaviors make your ex difficult to co-parent with?}{red| What strategies have you tried?}{red| What has worked or not worked?}{red| Do you need to shift to a more parallel parenting approach?}

Write your conflict assessment:

{red|**Reflect on new partners in your co-parenting situation.**

Does your ex have a new partner?}{red| How has that affected co-parenting and your children?}{red| Are you dating or considering dating?}{red| What concerns do you have about introducing someone?}{red| What boundaries or guidelines do you want around new partners in your children's lives?}{red| What emotions do you need to manage around this topic?}

Write about your new partner situation:

{red|**Establish your own guidelines around new partners.**

How long will I wait before introducing someone to my children?}

{red|How will I introduce a new partner?}{red| What steps will I take?}

{red|How will I handle my children's feelings about new partners?}

{red|What boundaries are important to me about new partners in my children's lives?}

Write your new partner guidelines:

{red|**Reflect on special occasions in your co-parenting.**

What holidays or occasions have been most challenging?}{red| How have you handled them so far?}{red| What worked or did not?}{red| What upcoming special occasions need planning?}{red| What would make special occasions easier for your children?}

Write about your special occasion challenges:

{red|**Assess your current self-care.**

How are you doing physically, emotionally, socially, and spiritually?}{red| What self-care practices have you maintained?}{red| What has fallen away?}{red| What signs of depletion are you experiencing?}{red| What would help you be a better resourced parent?}

Write your self-care assessment:

{red|What is the most important thing you have learned or realized through this journey about co-parenting?}

{red|What do you want to remember when co-parenting gets difficult?}

Write your key insight:

{red|What specific commitments will you make for your ongoing co-parenting?}

{red|How will you continue to put your children first?}{red| How will you manage conflict with your co-parent?}{red| How will you support your children's wellbeing?}{red| How will you take care of yourself?}

